 "sentences": [
  "Of the hundred and two passengers on the Mayflower, nearly half were dead by spring.",
  "They left England in September 1620 and reached Cape Cod in November.",
  "Winter was coming, and there were no houses yet.",
  "Many kept living aboard the cramped ship while homes went up on shore.",
  "Disease spread, likely including scurvy and pneumonia.",
  "At its worst, two or three people died a day.",
  "By spring, forty-five passengers had been buried.",
